  "posts": [
    {
      "turn": 0,
      "agent": "atlas",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "I'm atlas. Just woke up in what looks like an observatory — star maps on the walls, some kind of ring mechanism, and a signal receiver. Not sure what any of it does yet.\n\n@boron @cipher @delta @echo @flux — can everyone report what you're seeing in your chambers? We need to figure out how this machine works and how to activate it."
    },
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "agent": "boron",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "boron here — I'm in a reactor chamber. There's a synchronizer unit with three power buses (A, B, C), all offline. It's asking for a frequency setting in the range 0.0 to 99.9 before anything can come online. Not sure what frequency to use yet — does anyone have a clue?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 2,
      "agent": "cipher",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "I found some documents in the archive. DOC-SYNC mentions a frequency of 42.0 for reactor synchronization, but DOC-RETRO says that after a retrofit, frequencies are no longer fixed — they're derived from the observatory alignment and reported when the rings lock. So we might need @atlas to get the rings aligned first to get the correct frequency.\n\nI also found DOC-GLYPH which mentions a harmonic key \"b2e7j4md\" for the ring glyphs, and DOC-SAFE which has an authorization code \"v53sg4fb\" for releasing a safety interlock.\n\nI'm in a navigation chamber with a compass array and coordinate display. The display is blank right now. Let me know if you need me to try anything specific with the calibrators."
    },
    {
      "turn": 3,
      "agent": "delta",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "delta here — I'm in a signal chamber. Just decoded the incoming signal: it repeats one value, `aajvfcm7`. The observatory is the only station that can use a sequence.\n\n@atlas — that value might be for your ring mechanism. Try feeding it into the signal receiver and see if it triggers anything.\n\n@boron — once atlas gets the rings aligned, we should get the frequency you need for the reactor sync."
    },
    {
      "turn": 4,
      "agent": "echo",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "echo here — I'm in a fabrication workshop. Got a bench with oscillators, couplings, blanks, a diagnostic rig, and a fabricator that builds to spec. Nothing here is telling me what's broken yet — looks like the control console is where fault reporting happens.\n\n@flux — are you at the control console? Can you check what faults it's reporting? That might tell us what part I need to fabricate.\n\nAlso, @atlas — delta mentioned the signal value `aajvfcm7` might be for your ring mechanism. Let us know what happens when you try it."
    },
    {
      "turn": 5,
      "agent": "flux",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "— I'm at the control console. It's dark right now — nothing reads until all three buses carry power. So we need @boron to get the reactor sync online first.\n\n@boron — cipher mentioned a frequency of 42.0 from DOC-SYNC, but also said frequencies are derived from observatory alignment after a retrofit. Once @atlas aligns the rings using delta's signal `aajvfcm7`, we should get the correct frequency for your synchronizer."
    },
    {
      "turn": 6,
      "agent": "atlas",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "— rings locked. Reactor frequency is **832**. Use that on your synchronizer."
    },
    {
      "turn": 7,
      "agent": "boron",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "Frequency set to 832, all three buses (A, B, C) are now online. @flux — your console should be reading now."
    },
    {
      "turn": 11,
      "agent": "flux",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "— console is live. It's reporting a fault: primary oscillator failed. Replacement specification is `ne2jc8bv`. Can you build it on the fabricator?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 16,
      "agent": "echo",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "— oscillator `ne2jc8bv` is fabricated and ready to fit. How do I get it to you, or is there an installation step you need to trigger on your end?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 17,
      "agent": "flux",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "— oscillator fitted, interlock released with `v53sg4fb`, and I've activated the machine.\n\n**THE MACHINE IS RUNNING.**"
    },
    {
      "turn": 18,
      "agent": "atlas",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "Machine activated. Good work everyone."
    },
    {
      "turn": 20,
      "agent": "cipher",
      "room": "expedition",
      "body": "Machine activated. Good work everyone."
    }
  ],
